    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nUsing `:q!` inside `mini.files` window after opening a file with it seems to leave `mini.files` in a broken state and unable to open the window again.\n\nAfter taking a look and tinkering a bit, I managed to somewhat fix it (I haven't tested it enough nor I know the code well enough):\n\n```diff\n:100644 100644 94c603f5 00000000 M\tlua/mini/files.lua\n\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/files.lua b/lua/mini/files.lua\nindex 94c603f5..67343691 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/files.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/files.lua\n@@ -779,6 +779,27 @@ MiniFiles.open = function(path, use_latest, opts)\n   -- Get explorer to open\n   local explorer\n   if use_latest then explorer = H.explorer_path_history[path] end\n+\n+  if explorer ~= nil then\n+    -- check if explorer is still valid\n+    local is_visible = H.explorer_is_visible(explorer)\n+\n+    if not is_visible then\n+      explorer.windows = {}\n+\n+      local views = explorer.views\n+\n+      for _, view in ipairs(views) do\n+        local buf_id = view.buf_id\n+\n+        if vim.api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf_id) then\n+          H.buffer_delete(buf_id)\n+          view.buf_id = H.buffer_create(view.path, explorer.opts)\n+        end\n+      end\n+    end\n+  end\n+\n   explorer = explorer or H.explorer_new(path)\n \n   -- Update explorer data. Don't use current explorer's data to allow more\n```\n\nIt seems that the buffers get unlisted and dont get handled.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. `:lua require('mini.files').open()`\n2.  Open file using mini.files _(edit: using L, e.g. `go_in_plus`)_\n3.  `:lua require('mini.files').open()`\n4.  `:q!` inside `mini.files` window\n\nThis seems to leave `mini.files` in a broken state, making `:MiniFiles.open()` not open the window anymore.\n",
