            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nFor reference, the proper way to close explorer is [by pressing `q`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-files.txt#L153) or by executing [`MiniFiles.close()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-files.txt#L772).\n\nClosing a window only closes one single window, not the whole explorer. As this leads to a changed focus from the explorer windows, the rest get cleaned up after some time (no more than 1 second).\n\n> This seems to leave `mini.files` in a broken state, making `:MiniFiles.open()` not open the window anymore.\n\nI can not reproduce this part. Window closes as expected, the possible rest of the windows are closed a bit later. I can open explorer without any problems.\n\nCan you reproduce this behavior with *only* 'mini.files' set up? I.e. with suggested reproduction steps mentioned when creating a bug report?",
