            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> For reference, the proper way to close explorer is [by pressing `q`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-files.txt#L153) or by executing [`MiniFiles.close()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/088d67751584e4168f35bca89bad70ada7ea4636/doc/mini-files.txt#L772).\n\nYeah, i know, but sometimes i still hit it with `:q!` cause im used to it. It actually took me a while to know what was happening.\n\n\n> Can you reproduce this behavior with _only_ 'mini.files' set up? I.e. with suggested reproduction steps mentioned when creating a bug report?\n\nI already did that, sorry for not mentioning that.\n\nHere is a recording with `asciinema`:\n\n[![asciicast](https://asciinema.org/a/dC5aPL1oesncfW3tMAWrrTnmj.svg)](https://asciinema.org/a/dC5aPL1oesncfW3tMAWrrTnmj)\n\nHere some versioning info just in case:\n\n- NVIM v0.12.0-dev-248+g317a897c46\n- Linux 6.11.0-24-generic 24.04.1-Ubuntu x86_64\n\nI tested it on kitty and foot. Using zsh and bash.",
