        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "With this setup from @MariaSolOs your problem will be fixed:\n```lua\n  vim.keymap.set('n', '-', function()\n    local bufname = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0)\n    local path = vim.fn.fnamemodify(bufname, ':p')\n    if path and vim.uv.fs_stat(path) then\n      require('mini.files').open(bufname, false)\n    end\n  end)\n```\nI tested the quit from `mini.files` with `:q!` and opening it again several times and it behaves normally.\nThis configuration is also useful when opening a file, but not from `mini.files`, because it will open `mini.files` where you are and not in the root of the project. It will behave like vinegar.\nJust change the keymap to your keymap.\nThanks @echasnovski for the nice work.\n",
