        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`.\n\nThe issue was indeed that `close()` was doing nothing if there was no visible windows (as after `:q!` without enabled preview) and that is why I wasn't able to reproduce this initially (because I had enabled  preview). And thus resuming previously opened explorer resulted in some issues.\n\nThe reason [this solution](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1769#issuecomment-2848381432) worked was because it explicitly didn't use previously opened explorer state.",
            "created_at": "2025-05-05T13:46:47Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1769#issuecomment-2851069094",
