        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > The reason [this solution](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1769#issuecomment-2848381432) worked was because it explicitly didn't use previously opened explorer state.\n> \n> [@echasnovski](https://github.com/echasnovski) And so there should be no need to have those checks around `MiniFiles.open()` anymore?\n\nIf I understand correctly, the checks are about making sure that first argument to `open()` is a valid path. That is, to be able to press `-` even inside buffers for not actual file path.\n\nThis should have nothing to do with the merged fix, which could be observed only if the *second* argument is `true`.",
